{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget and round cap are both exhausted (400/400 evals, round 4 of 4), so no further exploration is possible. The front is feasible and well-covered: 237 feasible designs (204 unique), 30 on the Pareto front, spanning luts_plus_ffs 1227..4074 against an HV reference of 4000 and accuracy_bits 12..23.9 against an HV reference of 12, with hypervolume 1.866e+04 still gaining (+2.4%). All three constraints are comfortably met by the front's cheapest design (pipelined_m, data_width=19, n_iter=14, angle_guard=-2, frac_guard=1, trunc, m=3): throughput 119 MSPS >= 32, max_abs_err 2.41e-4 <= 2.44e-4, and sys_p99_batch_us best seen 0.154 <= 0.44. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) picks that 1227 LUT+FF design, which is the smallest feasible point found. No constraint is unreachable, so infeasible is not warranted; the front is good enough to stop."
